2026-05-20 11:39:14,216 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: ### Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, is pleased to submit a comprehensive tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval. Our proposal leverages our expertise in AI/ML systems, GDPR compliance, security, and sustainability to deliver a high-quality solution that meets the client's requirements.

### Understanding of Requirements
We have carefully reviewed the call for tenders and understand the need for an intelligent assistance tool that can facilitate access to information, improve answer quality, and reduce processing times. We acknowledge the regulatory constraints, including GDPR compliance, data protection, and explainability of AI recommendations. Our proposal addresses these requirements while ensuring a high level of availability, security, and sustainability.

### Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes a cloud-native design leveraging Outscale's SecNumCloud infrastructure, which meets the sovereignty requirement of hosting data within the EU. We will deploy a containerized application using Docker and Kubernetes, integrating with required APIs, including civil-status and town-planning software, EDM systems (such as Alfresco and Maarch Courrier), and user directories (like Active Directory and Keycloak). Our LLM model, Mistral 7B Instruct, will provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, while our explainability tools (SHAP and LIME) ensure transparency and accuracy.

To meet the performance requirement of a response time lower than 2 seconds, we will optimize our solution using quantization methods like INT8 or auto-scaling. We expect a p95 response time of approximately 1800ms, which is close to the required limit. Our high availability architecture design using Terraform and Ansible for infrastructure provisioning and configuration management will ensure an objective of 99.9% availability.

For GDPR compliance, we guarantee EU-only data hosting, encryption of sensitive data using anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, and implementation of access control standards, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC). Our Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA) capability will assess the impact of our AI-powered information systems on personal data protection.

Our subcontracting policy requires all subcontractors to be EU-established, reducing cross-border data flow risks. We have a source code escrow capability in place with Logitas, a French provider, to mitigate vendor lock-in risks. Our solution will also adhere to the principles of transparency, fairness, and accountability in AI decision-making processes as required by the EU AI Act.

The estimated annual revenue from this project is approximately 750,000 euros per year, based on a total contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years. We target a gross margin percentage of 28% and will focus on optimizing variable costs (65% of project costs) to ensure the expected service quality while maintaining a competitive price.

To reduce energetic consumption, we propose leveraging green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, which utilize 100% renewable energy. Our digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantization and auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, can reduce energetic consumption by approximately 35% compared to our baseline.

### Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender have been left unaddressed in our proposal.

### Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is committed to delivering a high-quality AI solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool. Our proposal combines expertise in AI/ML systems, GDPR compliance, security, and sustainability to provide a comprehensive solution that enhances municipal agents' daily missions while respecting regulatory constraints and minimizing environmental impact. We believe our solution offers significant value and look forward to the opportunity to implement it.
